-- title:
--   Lemma A.1 — good event
-- statement:
--   Run Algorithm 1 with the parameters of App. A.1. Let $G_k$ be the event that $P\in\mathcal P_{k'}$ for all $k'\le k$, and let $G=G_K$. Then $G_k$ is $\mathcal F_{k-1}$-measurable and
--   $$\Pr(G)\ge1-\delta/4.$$
--   Moreover, with the same bound, $P$ satisfies every constraint of (16) in every episode.
--
--   This is the high-probability event under which $q_k\le q^{\pi_k}$, which the lower occupancies of the algorithm rely on.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - generalization: G_k measurable and Pr(G) ≥ 1 − δ/4, for C a large constant → the same for every real C, and a further clause: Pr(P satisfies every constraint of (16) in every episode) ≥ 1 − δ/4; reason: β does not involve C and coverage does not depend on the policies; the further clause is what the paper's union bound proves, implies Pr(G) ≥ 1 − δ/4, and is needed by Lemmas A.13 and A.15
--   - encoding: episodes k = 1, …, K → 0-based episodes k < K; reason: Lean convention; same instances
--   - encoding: terminal layer S_H → no terminal layer: last-layer rows vanish and V, B are 0 beyond the last layer; reason: the paper merges S_H into one state, which affects neither q_k nor B_k (p.30)
--   - encoding: the agent's and the environment's randomness → a run of Algorithm 1 as a function of a uniform random tape; reason: one realization of the protocol; the statement depends only on the joint law of the run
--   - encoding: with probability at least 1 − p → μ(failure set) ≤ p; reason: outer-measure bound on the failure set; no measurability side condition is needed
--   - reading: F_k contains the history of episodes 1, …, k, including the agent's internal randomness → F_k is generated by the tape coordinates of these episodes; reason: it also contains coins the run never reads, which are independent of everything
-- source:
--   Kulkarni–Nguyen–Chang–Dai, Introducing Feedback Delays to Non-Delayed Adversarial MDPs, STOC 2027 submission (manuscript sha256 a639c54c…5e3530), Lemma A.1, p.29

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_IntroDelayAMDP_LayeredSpace
import Definitions.Def_IntroDelayAMDP_IsTransition
import Definitions.Def_IntroDelayAMDP_tabParams
import Definitions.Def_IntroDelayAMDP_tapeMeasure
import Definitions.Def_IntroDelayAMDP_tapeFilt
import Definitions.Def_IntroDelayAMDP_goodEvent
import Definitions.Def_IntroDelayAMDP_coverEvent

namespace IntroDelayAMDP

open MeasureTheory

/-- **Lemma A.1 (Good Event)** (printed p.29, of Kulkarni–Nguyen–Chang–Dai, *Introducing Feedback Delays to Non-Delayed Adversarial MDPs*, STOC 2027 submission (manuscript sha256 a639c54c…5e3530)): "Let `G_k` be the event that `P ∈ P_{k′}` for
all `k′ ≤ k`, and let `G ≜ G_K` be the good event. Then `G_k` is `F_{k−1}`-measurable, and
`Pr(G) ≥ 1 − δ/4`."

For Algorithm 1 run with the parameters `tabParams C 0 S A H K δ` on the tape: for every 0-based
episode `j < K` the event `goodEvent … j` (the paper's `G_{j+1}`) is measurable for `tapeFilt … j`
(the paper's `F_j`), and the complement of the good event `G = goodEvent … (K − 1)` has probability
at most `δ/4`. In addition, the complement of the smaller event `coverEvent … (K − 1)`, on which `P`
satisfies every constraint of (16) in every episode, has probability at most `δ/4`.

**Formalization Note.** Stated for every real `C`: the coverage of the confidence sets does not
depend on the policies, hence not on `C`. The last clause is what the paper's proof bounds (its union
bound runs over all constraints); it is stated because Lemmas A.13 and A.15 need it (see their
notes), and it implies the second clause. -/
theorem lemma_A_1 :
    ∀ (St A : Type) [Fintype St] [DecidableEq St] [Fintype A] [Nonempty A] (H K : ℕ)
      (L : LayeredSpace St H) (P : St → A → St → ℝ), IsTransition L P →
      ∀ ℓ : ℕ → St → A → ℝ, (∀ k < K, ∀ s a, 0 ≤ ℓ k s a ∧ ℓ k s a ≤ 1) →
      ∀ δ : ℝ, 0 < δ → δ < 1 → 1 ≤ K →
      ∀ C : ℝ, let p := tabParams C 0 (Fintype.card St) (Fintype.card A) H K δ
      (∀ j < K, MeasurableSet[tapeFilt St A K H j] (goodEvent K L P ℓ p j)) ∧
        tapeMeasure St A K H (goodEvent K L P ℓ p (K - 1))ᶜ ≤ ENNReal.ofReal (δ / 4) ∧
        tapeMeasure St A K H (coverEvent K L P ℓ p (K - 1))ᶜ ≤ ENNReal.ofReal (δ / 4) := by sorry

end IntroDelayAMDP
